==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|militia|mīlitia|military, military service|lang=la}}, from {{term|miles|mīles|soldier|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-militia.ogg|Audio (US)}}

*: {{rhymes|ɪʃə}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[army]] of [[train]]ed [[civilian]]s, which may be an [[official]] [[reserve]] army, called upon in time of need; the national [[police force]] of a country; the entire [[able-bodied]] [[population]] of a state; or a [[private]] force, not under [[government]] [[control]].

